      "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<0.75).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "If $Z∼N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<0.75)=P(Z\\le 0.75)=Φ(0.75).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/2541e696df1d871e65d3717d03c2ce842f4312c6a86fd09ccc8f13e04d8d1216.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(0.75)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $0.7$ and the column that corresponds to $0.05.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 0.75)=Φ(0.75)=0.7734.\n$$",
